<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade-June 14.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade-June 14.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended June 14:</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     320	   1.35     539000  172.48   22.00</p>
<p>State Bank	   320	  15.27     482700  154.46   62.20</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   183	   0.65     514750   94.20    4.63</p>
<p>HDFC		  3440	  15.17	13360   45.96    5.75</p>
<p>Colgate		300	   1.31     110500   33.15   22.77</p>
<p>HLL		   1300	   5.53	24800   32.24   22.18</p>
<p>BHEL		   390	   1.81	78500   30.62   24.20</p>
<p>ACC		   1205	   4.94	25310   30.50   21.38</p>
<p>Tata Tea	     345	  11.07	84250   29.07   41.83</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   895	  24.15	27800   24.88   35.17</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 27.67 percent on an annualised basis against 11.13 percent in the previous carry forward account ended June 7.</p>
